    "title": "Search for $\\boldsymbol{B \\to h \\nu \\bar{\\nu}}$ Decays with Semileptonic Tagging at Belle",
    "arxiv": "[hep-ex/1702.03224v3](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1702.03224)",
    "time": "2017.02.10",
    "abstract": "We present the results of a search for the rare decays $B \\to h \\nu \\overline{\\nu}$, where $h$ stands for $K^+,$ $K^0_{\\mathrm{S}},$ $K^{*+},$ $K^{*0},$ $\\pi^+,$ $\\pi^0,$ $\\rho^+$ and $\\rho^0$, using the full Belle data sample of $772 \\times 10^6$ $B \\bar{B}$ pairs collected at the $\\Upsilon(4S)$ resonance with the Belle detector at the KEKB asymmetric-energy $e^+ e^-$ collider. We find no significant signal and set upper limits on the branching fractions.",
    "pdf": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1702.03224",
